I have a similar system (SX164 with MilleniumII and 128Mb)

> 1) under Gnome(I havent run anything else yet) the curser in an Xterm
> session seems to display a very strange overlay when the cursor
> dissapears. If I move the mouse the overlay dissapears and the regular
> cursor comes back.

I have not had a problem with this - cursor dissappears when I start
typing and reappears when I move the mouse as it should - Xserver?

> 2)Gnome seems to generate a high number of core dumps. 

... and then some! I always end up with one on the desktop, which I have
yet to track down.

> 3) I have had gnome effectivly lock up so tha I was unable to create new
> windows. I could still move around between open windows but I could not
> open any new ones.

Okay... I sorted this by recompiling the kernel - I am fairly sure it is
to do with the fontserver, but recompilation with no modules seems to
have fixed this problem. There is probably a better solution.

> 4) xfm seems to die. 

Not tried.. don't use.

