Ok.. here is some info:

Linux xxxxx 2.2.7 #4 Sun Jun 6 00:46:51 PDT 1999 alpha
unknown

32 root#/sbin/depmod -av | grep smb
/lib/modules/2.2.7/fs/smbfs.o

33 root#rpm -qa | grep samba
samba-2.0.3-2

I then issue the command:

/etc/rc.d/init.d/smb start

and then:

smbmount //NetBios_Name/Share -c 'mount /mnt/point' -U
username

enter passwd when prompted... and then I get:

44 root#df
Filesystem         1024-blocks  Used Available
Capacity Mounted on
/dev/sda3            4155375 1354072  2586256     34% 
 /
/dev/sdb1            4290196 1900321  2167886     47% 
 /u
//NETBIOS_NAME/SHARE      538240  169776   368464    
32%   /mnt/point

I'm assuming that is what you are trying to do? If
not, sorry for the junk.... if so, be hopeful that it
does work.

I don't remember anymore, but I think I did recompile
samba myself... and didn't use a pre-compiled RPM.

Good Luck,
D.


