> Was looking around ebay and saw a listing for a DEC Alpha 21040. 
> I haven't heard anything about that particular chip, and was unable to
> find any details about it on the digital page or the alphalinux page.
> Anyone know anything about it?
> 
>                                    - Aakin
> 
> -- 
> To unsubscribe: send e-mail to axp-list-request@redhat.com with
> 'unsubscribe' as the subject.  Do not send it to axp-list@redhat.com

Yeah. It is an ethernet controller, from the DEC "Tulip" family, and is only
capable of 10Mbit ethernet (you need a 2114x for 100Mbit). Not a processor I'm
afraid - as far as I can tell processors are all 21x6x numbers, ethernet
controllers are 21x4x, PCI bridges are 21x5x and motherboard core logic
chipsets are 21x7x.

Cheers,

	David


