Hi Izaak !

On Tue, Jun 29, 1999 at 10:53:48PM -0400, Izaak Bozof wrote:
> I am looking to burn a couple of install cd's, but I don't know what the fs
> that is required to boot from SRM.  iso9660 only supports "compatible" 8.3
> filenames.
> 
> Is there an FAQ/HOWTO on this somewhere?

I don't know if there is a FAQ. But how to create a bootable
SRM-compatible CD is described in the documentation that is included
with aboot. You simply use is9660 with rockridge extensions
and use isomarkboot on that image.

Maybe my old Makefile can help you. I've used it to create our
distribution CD's (the old one had only a big tarball in it).
It should be self-explaining.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Create Quant-X distribution
#

PWD=$(shell pwd)
ISOIMG=$(PWD)/../../CDIMAGE.ISO
TAR_BASE=$(PWD)/../../new_tgz
INSTALLER=$(PWD)/../../new_installer
BOOTLX=/boot/bootlx

MKISOFS=/usr/bin/mkisofs
CDRECORD=/usr/lib/xcdroast-0.96d/bin/cdrecord-1.6
ISOMARKBOOT=/sbin/isomarkboot

all: $(ISOIMG)


$(ISOIMG): $(INSTALLER)/system.tgz
	-cp -f $(BOOTLX) $(INSTALLER)/
	$(MKISOFS) -a -l -J -L -o $@ -R -r -T -v $(INSTALLER)
	-isomarkboot $@ bootlx

$(INSTALLER)/system.tgz:
	rm -f $@
	( cd $(TAR_BASE) ; tar zcpf $@ .[a-zA-Z]* * )

burn: $(ISOIMG)
	$(CDRECORD) dev=1,3,0 speed=2 -v -v -v $(ISOIMG)
----------------------------------------------------------------------


